$ WHEELHOUSE_REAL_PI_PROVIDER=openai-codex WHEELHOUSE_REAL_PI_MODEL=gpt-5.5 bash seats/concurrency.selftest.sh

1. two seats, one roster — spawn, overlap, isolation, clean stop
  ok    hermetic: worker-a spawns
  ok    hermetic: worker-b spawns
  ok    hermetic: each seat has its OWN FIFO (worker-a.stdin, worker-b.stdin)
  ok    hermetic: bead-a dispatched to worker-a
  ok    hermetic: bead-b dispatched to worker-b (before bead-a's turn ended)
  ok    hermetic: overlapping RUNNING — both state.json pids alive at once (51564, 52063)
  ok    hermetic: both turns in flight at the same moment (agent_start seen, no agent_end yet, both logs)
  ok    hermetic: status shows both seats RUNNING
  ok    hermetic: worker-a's turn finished
  ok    hermetic: worker-b's turn finished
  ok    hermetic: worker-a's events land ONLY in worker-a's log
  ok    hermetic: worker-b's events land ONLY in worker-b's log
  ok    hermetic: each bead's work landed only in its own worktree
  ok    hermetic: the two worktrees are on distinct fleet/<bead> branches
  ok    hermetic: worker-a stops cleanly
  ok    hermetic: worker-b stops cleanly

1b. state.json concurrent writers preserve both seat records
  ok    race: concurrent spawns both exit 0
  ok    race: re-read-before-merge preserves both seat records in state.json

2. capacity visibility — a quota-shaped failure is stamped and rendered
  ok    quota-shaped dispatch fails loudly
  ok    state.json records lastCapacityEvent with the failure detail: {"at":"2026-09-10T17:05:41.356Z","detail":"429 rate limit exceeded — usage limit reached for this account"}
  ok    adapter status surfaces the capacity event
  ok    floor --once renders the AMBER PARKED/QUOTA line with the re-probe command
  ok    floor STATUS cell shows per-account capacity state
  ok    a dispatch that lands clears the capacity event

3. canary — can these checks detect broken isolation and a lost stamp?
  ok    canary: an adapter that merges both seats into one log is caught
  ok    canary: an adapter with the capacity stamp cut is caught (no lastCapacityEvent lands)

